{"name":"Malmö FF","hex":"#a7d7ff","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Malmö FF","blocks":[{"text":"Malmö Fotbollförening, commonly known simply as Malmö FF or MFF, is a Swedish professional football club based in Malmö, Scania. They compete in the Allsvenskan, the top division of Swedish football, and play home matches at the Eleda Stadion. Malmö FF is Sweden's most successful football club in terms of domestic trophies won. They hold 24 Swedish championships and 16 Svenska Cupen titles, both of which are national records."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Malmo_FF_logo.svg/330px-Malmo_FF_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malm%C3%B6_FF","wikidata":"Q204881"},{"title":"Malmö FF (women)","blocks":[{"text":"Malmö Fotbollförening, commonly known as Malmö FF, Malmö, or MFF, are a women's association football team from Malmö, who compete in the Damallsvenskan, the highest level of women's football in Sweden. Formed on 26 November 2019 and affiliated with the Scania Football Association, Malmö FF are based in Malmö, Scania."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Malmo_FF_logo.svg/330px-Malmo_FF_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malm%C3%B6_FF_(women)","wikidata":"Q85783500"},{"title":"Malmö","blocks":[{"text":"Malmö is the third-largest city in Sweden, after Stockholm and Gothenburg, and the seventh-largest city in the Nordic region. Located on the Öresund strait on the southwestern coast of Sweden, it is the largest city in Scania, with a municipal population of 365,644 in 2024, and is the gubernatorial seat of Skåne County. Malmö received its city privileges in 1353, and today Malmö's metropolitan region is home to over 700,000 people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Malm%C3%B6%E2%80%93flygbild_06_september_2014.jpg/330px-Malm%C3%B6%E2%80%93flygbild_06_september_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malm%C3%B6","wikidata":"Q2211"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/GamlaIP.jpg/500px-GamlaIP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/GamlaIP.jpg/500px-GamlaIP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Malmö IP, the first home stadium for the club between 1910 and 1957","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGamlaIP.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Guldlaget1944.jpg/500px-Guldlaget1944.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Guldlaget1944.jpg/500px-Guldlaget1944.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Malmö FF team of 1943–44","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGuldlaget1944.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Malmoffplayers1962.jpg/330px-Malmoffplayers1962.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Malmoffplayers1962.jpg/330px-Malmoffplayers1962.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Young players in the 1960s","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMalmoffplayers1962.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Sweden_malm%C3%B6_stadion_sweden.jpg/500px-Sweden_malm%C3%B6_stadion_sweden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Sweden_malm%C3%B6_stadion_sweden.jpg/1280px-Swe